      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Holocaust Denial/Minimization",
      "description": "The text overlay 'the horrors of the holocaust three u.s. soldiers look at bodies' is a direct counter to Holocaust denial/minimization themes. The image, depicting U.S. soldiers observing bodies in a crematorium, is meant to convey the gravity of the event, not to be dismissed or minimized. The meme manifests toxicity by potentially trivializing or misrepresenting the Holocaust through its framing, which could be interpreted as minimizing the scale or horror of the genocide.",
